<title>GREECE: XIOSBANK CUTS AUTO LOAN RATES BY 125 BPS.</title>
<headline>XIOSBANK CUTS AUTO LOAN RATES BY 125 BPS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Xiosbank, which has filed</p>
<p>for listing on the Athens bourse, will cut its auto loans for</p>
<p>new and used cars by 125 basis points to 18.50 percent and 20.50</p>
<p>percent, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank will keep its base rate for business credit steady</p>
<p>at 18.75 percent for a week effective Monday, it said.</p>
<p>Its Xios Alma account will offer annual returns of 11.57</p>
<p>percent and monthly payments of interest, it added.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
